   b) build the Program from source for personal review on your own device, without giving the build to anyone else;
   c) quote parts of the code in bug and vulnerability reports sent to CubeXCraft.

3. Without written permission from CubeXCraft you may not:
   a) copy, distribute, publish, sell or otherwise transfer the Program, its parts or builds, in source or executable
      form;
   b) modify the Program and distribute modified versions, or create derivative works based on it, including launchers
      for other servers or projects;
   c) use the CubeXCraft name, logos, graphics, interface design, texts or other CubeXCraft materials;
   d) remove or alter copyright notices or this license;
   e) use the Program or its parts to bypass protection, access other people's accounts or break the CubeXCraft rules.

4. Official builds are distributed only through https://www.cubexcraft.site and the built-in update and are signed with
   the CubeX certificate (SHA-256 98b07a07f3d533e764e17ca876474554fe385debb9a54add910c97200a9ce813). Their use is
   governed by the CubeXCraft rules.

5. The `core/` library and third-party components are distributed under their own licenses (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
   This license does not restrict the rights those licenses grant. In particular, under the LGPL you may modify the
   `core/` library, build the Program with the modified library, and reverse-engineer the Program as far as needed to
